From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:50:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] BD-J: BD-Live setting, Internet addresses only, sockets
 on every Java

BD-Live, the network for the Java code of a disc, as a player setting that is off by default:
BLURAY_PLAYER_SETTING_BDJ_NETWORK (0x1100), BLURAY_BDJ_NETWORK_NONE or _INTERNET,
BD_HAVE_BDJ_NETWORK_SETTING. It is kept in BDJ_CONFIG.network_internet and taken when the JVM
is created; with it off a disc is told bluray.network.connected=NO and every connection is
refused.

Which addresses: IPv4 of the Internet only. bdlive_net.c and org.videolan.NetAddress hold the same
table: the IPv4 ranges that are not globally reachable (IANA's special-purpose registry: this
network, RFC 1918, carrier-grade NAT, loopback, link-local, IETF assignments, documentation, 6to4
relays, benchmarking), multicast, reserved and broadcast; and the addresses and on-link subnets of
this system's own interfaces. No IPv6: on a home network every device has global IPv6 addresses
in the prefix of this system, so no rule on an address tells the network (or this system, where
the player listens) from the Internet.

libbluray's sockets did not work from Java 13 on: BDJSocketFactory built java.net.SocksSocketImpl
through reflection with a constructor those versions do not have (NoSuchMethodException on 17, 21
and 26; libbluray master too). BDJSocketImpl is a SocketImpl on a SocketChannel and the Socket it
adapts, with public API only, the same on every Java from 1.4 on. Each connection is checked on
the address it goes to, after its name is resolved, and said in the log (on the critical path, so
that the player shows it): "BD-Live: connection to <name>:<port> (<address>) allowed", "refused:
<why>" or "failed". It binds, listens and accepts nothing; datagram sockets do not come through
the factory and are refused below (the server's filter). BDJSockets closes these sockets when the
Xlet ends, which its reflection on SocketImpl.getSocket() no longer could.
